  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "d5wf2d-sticky1",
      "name": "D5-WF2d Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        60,
        80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## D5-WF2d — Post-Call Processor (End-of-Call Handler)\n\nCalled **asynchronously** by D5-WF2b after VAPI fires end-of-call-report. No VAPI response needed.\n\n**Outcome routing:**\n- interested-callback → Reactivation Log (interested-callback) + D5 Callback Queue + Alert owner\n- not-interested → Reactivation Log (declined-final)\n- strong-dnc → Reactivation Log (opted-out) + Clients (do-not-contact, SMS Opt-Out=Y, Upcoming Appointment cleared) + Alert owner\n- no-answer → Retry logic (retry-pending if currentAttemptCount < maxAttempts, else exhausted)\n- already-terminal (booked/opted-out/interested-callback/declined-final/exhausted/completed) → update transcript URL only\n- unknown → log error\n\n**Attempt Count ownership:** WF2 is the sole incrementer. WF2d never writes Attempt Count.",
        "color": 4,
        "width": 760,
        "height": 300
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "d5wf2d-sticky2",
      "name": "Outcome Branches",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1460,
        80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Outcome Branch Notes\n\n**DNC write rule:** Only strong-dnc propagates to Clients. not-interested stays in D5 only.\n**Retry rule:** condition is currentAttemptCount < maxAttempts (WF2 already set count=1 after first call, so 1<2=retry, 2<2=exhausted).\n**Composite key:** Reactivation Log always matched on [Phone + Campaign ID].",
        "color": 5,
        "width": 400,
        "height": 200
      }
    },
